    "created_by": "leonardmarcq",
    "output": "Absolutely, it's really interesting! One standout example is Patagonia, which has long been committed to environmental sustainability. They not only use recycled materials for their products but also encourage customers to repair rather than replace their gear. Another great example is Unilever, which has made significant strides with its Sustainable Living Plan, aiming to reduce the company's environmental footprint while increasing its positive social impact. These companies illustrate how integrating corporate social responsibility can be both ethical and beneficial for business. What about you? Have you come across any companies that are doing a great job in this area?",
